refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.parameters;
flags
A bitmask of the CachingIterator constants. At most one of CachingIterator::CALL_TOSTRING, CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_KEY, CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_CURRENT and CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_INNER may be given.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws a ValueError if flags contains more than one of CachingIterator::CALL_TOSTRING, CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_KEY, CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_CURRENT and CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_INNER.
Throws an InvalidArgumentException if CachingIterator::CALL_TOSTRING or CachingIterator::TOSTRING_USE_INNER is currently set and flags does not contain it, as these flags cannot be unset.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.0.0

     Now throws a ValueError if
     flags contains more than one of the string
     conversion flags; previously, an
     InvalidArgumentException was thrown.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Turning on the full cache


<?php
$iterator = new CachingIterator(new ArrayIterator(['a', 'b', 'c']), 0);
$iterator->setFlags(CachingIterator::FULL_CACHE);

foreach ($iterator as $value) {
    // ...
}

var_dump($iterator->getCache());
?>


   &example.outputs;


array(3) {
  [0]=>
  string(1) "a"
  [1]=>
  string(1) "b"
  [2]=>
  string(1) "c"
}
